ROUGHLY 55,000 EMPLOYEES AND

00:15:49.948 --> 00:15:52.117
RECEIVED ON AVERAGE, BETWEEN 150

00:15:52.184 --> 00:15:53.752
TO 300 COMPLAINTS PER YEAR.

00:15:53.819 --> 00:15:56.055
BETWEEN 2018 AND 2022, TOTALING

00:15:56.121 --> 00:15:59.391
MORE THAN 1200 REPORTS OF SEXUAL

00:15:59.458 --> 00:16:01.527
HARASSMENT CLAIMS AGAINST CSU

00:16:01.593 --> 00:16:02.528
EMPLOYEES. AND THE CSU

00:16:02.594 --> 00:16:04.663
INVESTIGATED 254 OF THESE

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:07.366
REPORTS, OR ROUGHLY 20% OF ALL

00:16:07.433 --> 00:16:10.035
COMPLAINTS, AND SUBSTANTIATED

00:16:10.102 --> 00:16:12.705
SEXUAL HARASSMENT ALLEGATIONS IN

00:16:12.771 --> 00:16:14.873
98 OF THE 254 INVESTIGATIONS, OR

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:17.309
ROUGHLY 39% OF THE TIME WHEN

00:16:17.376 --> 00:16:19.845
APPROVING THE AUDIT REQUEST,

00:16:19.912 --> 00:16:21.480
JLAC DIRECTED MY OFFICE, AMONG

00:16:21.547 --> 00:16:23.515
OTHER THINGS, TO REVIEW THE ROLE

00:16:23.582 --> 00:16:25.484
OF THE CSU SYSTEM'S TITLE NINE

00:16:25.551 --> 00:16:27.286
OFFICES OFFICE IN TERMS OF ITS

00:16:27.353 --> 00:16:28.787
POLICIES AND PRACTICES. THEY

00:16:28.854 --> 00:16:31.223
ASKED US TO REVIEW THE CSU'S

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:31.757
PROCESS FOR INVESTIGATING

00:16:31.824 --> 00:16:34.159
ALLEGED SEXUAL HARASSMENT AND

00:16:34.226 --> 00:16:34.693
WHETHER THE INVESTIGATION

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:36.729
PROCESS WAS FREE FROM

00:16:36.795 --> 00:16:37.796
INTERFERENCE. THEY ASKED US TO

00:16:37.863 --> 00:16:39.798
LOOK AT THE REASONABLENESS OF

00:16:39.865 --> 00:16:40.799
THE DISCIPLINE IMPOSED AND ALSO

00:16:40.866 --> 00:16:42.468
TO EXAMINE CSU'S POLICIES FOR

00:16:42.534 --> 00:16:44.636
RETREAT RIGHTS AND LETTERS OF

00:16:44.703 --> 00:16:45.270
RECOMMENDATIONS FOR INDIVIDUALS

00:16:45.337 --> 00:16:48.107
WHO HAD FOUND TO HAVE ENGAGED IN

00:16:48.173 --> 00:16:51.009
SEXUAL HARASSMENT. OUR AUDIT

00:16:51.076 --> 00:16:52.044
REPORT, ALTHOUGH WE OBTAINED A

00:16:52.111 --> 00:16:54.012
LOT OF SYSTEM WIDE DATA THAT WE

00:16:54.079 --> 00:16:55.147
INCLUDE IN THE APPENDICES OF OUR

00:16:55.214 --> 00:16:57.015
REPORT, MOST OF OUR WORK FOCUSED

00:16:57.082 --> 00:16:58.617
ON A SELECTION OF 40 SEXUAL

00:16:58.684 --> 00:17:01.754
HARASSMENT COMPLAINTS PERTAINING

00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:02.988
TO EMPLOYEES AT THE CHANCELLOR'S

00:17:03.055 --> 00:17:05.124
OFFICE IN THREE CAMPUSES, WHICH

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:06.225
WERE FRESNO STATE, SAN JOSE

00:17:06.291 --> 00:17:08.060
STATE AND SONOMA STATE. AND

00:17:08.127 --> 00:17:10.629
OVERALL, OUR AUDIT FOUND

00:17:10.696 --> 00:17:11.764
WEAKNESSES AT BOTH THE CAMPUS

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:13.932
LEVEL AND THE SYSTEM WIDE LEVEL

00:17:13.999 --> 00:17:15.968
THAT COULD BE CATEGORIZED INTO

00:17:16.034 --> 00:17:16.969
THREE MAIN PROBLEMS THAT WE

00:17:17.035 --> 00:17:19.171
HIGHLIGHT IN OUR AUDIT REPORT.

00:17:19.238 --> 00:17:21.373
FIRST, WE CONCLUDED THAT THE CSU

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:22.441
CAMPUSES WE VISITED STRUGGLED TO

00:17:22.508 --> 00:17:24.343
ADEQUATELY AND CONSISTENTLY

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:25.110
INVESTIGATE ALLEGATIONS OF

00:17:25.177 --> 00:17:27.179
SEXUAL HARASSMENT. SECOND, WE

00:17:27.246 --> 00:17:29.581
FOUND THAT CAMPUSES COULD NOT

00:17:29.648 --> 00:17:30.582
ALWAYS DEMONSTRATE THAT THEY

00:17:30.649 --> 00:17:32.484
CONSISTENTLY IMPOSED DISCIPLINE.

00:17:32.551 --> 00:17:33.552
AND THIRD, WE FOUND THAT A

00:17:33.619 --> 00:17:35.387
SIGNIFICANT CAUSE FOR THESE

00:17:35.454 --> 00:17:37.122
INCONSISTENCIES WAS THE LACK OF

00:17:37.189 --> 00:17:38.524
SYSTEM WIDE GUIDANCE AND

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:39.491
MONITORING BY THE FORMER

00:17:39.558 --> 00:17:41.427
CHANCELLOR'S OFFICE. I'LL TALK

00:17:41.493 --> 00:17:44.062
BRIEFLY A LITTLE BIT ABOUT THE

00:17:44.129 --> 00:17:45.197
CONTENTS OF OUR REPORT BEFORE

00:17:45.264 --> 00:17:46.465
MOVING INTO THE RECOMMENDATIONS.

00:17:46.532 --> 00:17:49.435
WITH RESPECT TO THE FIRST POINT

00:17:49.501 --> 00:17:51.069
ON THE INCONSISTENT APPROACH TO

00:17:51.136 --> 00:17:52.070
INVESTIGATING CLAIMS OF SEXUAL

00:17:52.137 --> 00:17:54.573
HARASSMENT, WE NOTED A VARIETY

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:56.008
OF PROBLEMS IN THIS AREA, AND

00:17:56.074 --> 00:17:57.109
PROBABLY ONE OF THE MOST

00:17:57.176 --> 00:17:58.076
IMPORTANT ONES WAS THE

00:17:58.143 --> 00:17:58.944
UNEXPLAINED CLOSURE OF

00:17:59.011 --> 00:18:01.246
COMPLAINTS WITHOUT CONDUCTING

00:18:01.313 --> 00:18:01.880
INVESTIGATIONS, DECIDING WHETHER

00:18:01.947 --> 00:18:04.416
OR NOT TO CONDUCT AN

00:18:04.483 --> 00:18:06.251
INVESTIGATION IS ONE OF THE MOST

00:18:06.318 --> 00:18:07.419
CRITICAL STEPS IN RESPONDING TO

00:18:07.486 --> 00:18:09.121
AN ALLEGATION. IT'S ONLY THROUGH

00:18:09.188 --> 00:18:10.856
THE INVESTIGATION PROCESS THAT

00:18:10.923 --> 00:18:13.325
YOU CAN DETERMINE WHETHER OR NOT

00:18:13.392 --> 00:18:14.326
SEXUAL HARASSMENT HAS OCCURRED,

00:18:14.393 --> 00:18:16.128
AND THEREFORE, WHETHER OR NOT

00:18:16.195 --> 00:18:18.397
DISCIPLINE IS WARRANTED. IN 11

00:18:18.464 --> 00:18:19.731
OF THE 15 COMPLAINTS WE REVIEWED

00:18:19.798 --> 00:18:21.467
WERE CSU OFFICIALS CLOSED

00:18:21.533 --> 00:18:24.136
COMPLAINTS AT INTAKE WITHOUT

00:18:24.203 --> 00:18:25.070
CONDUCTING AN INVESTIGATION. WE

00:18:25.137 --> 00:18:27.573
FOUND THAT THE CSU OFFICIALS

00:18:27.639 --> 00:18:28.640
LACKED CLEAR RATIONALES FOR

00:18:28.707 --> 00:18:31.677
DOING SO. WE FOUND INSTANCES

00:18:31.743 --> 00:18:33.812
WHERE THEY PREMATURELY CONCLUDED

00:18:33.879 --> 00:18:34.947
THAT THE ALLEGED BEHAVIOR DIDN'T

00:18:35.013 --> 00:18:37.015
CONSTITUTE SEXUAL HARASSMENT,

00:18:37.082 --> 00:18:38.116
WHICH WE FOUND CONCERNING GIVEN

00:18:38.183 --> 00:18:39.485
THE NATURE OF THE ALLEGATIONS

00:18:39.551 --> 00:18:40.752
PRESENTED, WE FOUND THAT CSU

00:18:40.819 --> 00:18:42.888
OFFICIALS DID NOT ALWAYS

00:18:42.955 --> 00:18:43.922
DOCUMENT THE RATIONALE FOR

00:18:43.989 --> 00:18:46.024
CLOSING CASES AND WE ALSO NOTED

00:18:46.091 --> 00:18:47.159
NOTED INSTANCES WHERE THERE

00:18:47.226 --> 00:18:49.528
WASN'T ANY CLEAR ATTEMPT TO

00:18:49.595 --> 00:18:50.529
CONTACT OTHER INDIVIDUALS CITED

00:18:50.596 --> 00:18:52.831
IN THE ALLEGATION, BASED ON

00:18:52.898 --> 00:18:53.966
MATERIALS THAT WE FOUND IN THE

00:18:54.032 --> 00:18:55.634
CASE FILE. IMPORTANTLY, WE ALSO

00:18:55.701 --> 00:18:57.469
COULD NOT ALWAYS DETERMINE WHICH

00:18:57.536 --> 00:18:58.403
CAMPUS OFFICIALS DECIDED TO

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:00.172
CLOSE A CASE PRIOR TO AN

00:19:00.239 --> 00:19:02.541
INVESTIGATION BECAUSE CSU

00:19:02.608 --> 00:19:03.575
POLICIES DID NOT REQUIRE A

00:19:03.642 --> 00:19:06.411
SIGNATURE OR AN APPROVAL

00:19:06.478 --> 00:19:07.479
PROCESS, AND AS A RESULT, IT

00:19:07.546 --> 00:19:09.448
WASN'T ALWAYS CLEAR WHO HAD

00:19:09.515 --> 00:19:10.516
ACCOUNTABILITY FOR THE DECISIONS

00:19:10.582 --> 00:19:12.251
TO CLOSE CASES PRIOR TO AN

00:19:12.317 --> 00:19:14.953
INVESTIGATION. CSU'S POLICIES

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:15.954
REQUIRE TITLE NINE COORDINATORS

00:19:16.021 --> 00:19:17.856
TO DOCUMENT IN WRITING THE

00:19:17.923 --> 00:19:18.857
DECISIONS ABOUT WHETHER TO

00:19:18.924 --> 00:19:20.492
CONDUCT AN INVESTIGATION, BUT

00:19:20.559 --> 00:19:23.629
THE POLICY DIDN'T REQUIRE ANY

00:19:23.695 --> 00:19:24.630
DOCUMENTED RATIONALE FOR THIS

00:19:24.696 --> 00:19:27.032
IMPORTANT DECISION, WHICH IS IN

00:19:27.099 --> 00:19:28.934
CONTRAST TO GUIDANCE WE SAW FROM

00:19:29.001 --> 00:19:30.068
THE US DEPARTMENT OF JUSTICE

00:19:30.135 --> 00:19:31.303
WITH OTHER CAMPUSES AND THEIR

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:32.204
SETTLEMENT AGREEMENTS, FOR

00:19:32.271 --> 00:19:33.338
EXAMPLE, WITH SAN JOSE STATE,

00:19:33.405 --> 00:19:36.074
WHICH REQUIRES CLEAR DOCUMENTED

00:19:36.141 --> 00:19:37.075
RATIONALES FOR NOT PROCEEDING

00:19:37.142 --> 00:19:39.344
WITH AN INVESTIGATION OF SEXUAL

00:19:39.411 --> 00:19:40.312
HARASSMENT. MOVING TO THE

00:19:40.379 --> 00:19:42.614
INVESTIGATIONS THEMSELVES, WE

00:19:42.681 --> 00:19:43.649
ALSO FOUND INCONSISTENCIES THAT

00:19:43.715 --> 00:19:45.384
LED US TO QUESTION THE

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:46.485
CONCLUSIONS THAT WERE REACHED BY

00:19:46.552 --> 00:19:48.420
CSU OFFICIALS. WE NOTED

00:19:48.487 --> 00:19:50.455
WEAKNESSES IN SEVEN OF THE 21

00:19:50.522 --> 00:19:51.456
INVESTIGATIONS WE REVIEWED, AND

00:19:51.523 --> 00:19:53.825
EACH OF THOSE RESULTED IN CSU

00:19:53.892 --> 00:19:54.826
CONCLUDING THAT SEXUAL

00:19:54.893 --> 00:19:58.730
HARASSMENT ALLEGATIONS WERE NOT

00:19:58.797 --> 00:19:59.798
SUBSTANTIATED. AT EACH OF THE

00:19:59.865 --> 00:20:00.933
FOUR LOCATIONS WE VISITED, WE

00:20:00.999 --> 00:20:02.734
ENCOUNTERED SITUATIONS WHERE CSU

00:20:02.801 --> 00:20:04.803
OFFICIALS APPEARED TO USE AN

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:05.304
UNREASONABLY RESTRICTIVE

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:07.839
INTERPRETATION OF CSU'S

00:20:07.906 --> 00:20:10.609
DEFINITION OF SEXUAL HARASSMENT.

00:20:10.676 --> 00:20:11.777
FOR EXAMPLE, IN ONE CASE, A CSU

00:20:11.843 --> 00:20:13.912
EMPLOYEE PHYSICALLY TOUCHED A

00:20:13.979 --> 00:20:15.547
COMPLAINANT'S STOMACH AND HIP IN

00:20:15.614 --> 00:20:17.883
AN INTIMATE WAY AND SAID HE

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:19.017
THOUGHT THEY WOULD ALWAYS HAVE

00:20:19.084 --> 00:20:20.986
SEX. BUT THE CSU INVESTIGATOR

00:20:21.053 --> 00:20:22.387
WHO CONCLUDED THESE EVENTS DID

00:20:22.454 --> 00:20:23.589
OCCUR FOUND THAT THE CONDUCT WAS

00:20:23.655 --> 00:20:25.657
NOT SUFFICIENTLY SEVERE,

00:20:25.724 --> 00:20:28.160
PERSISTENT OR PERVASIVE. WE ALSO

00:20:28.226 --> 00:20:31.430
FOUND ISSUES WITH INVESTIGATORS

00:20:31.496 --> 00:20:32.364
OMITTING PARTS OF ALLEGATIONS

00:20:32.431 --> 00:20:34.299
FROM THE INVESTIGATION'S FINAL

00:20:34.366 --> 00:20:37.135
ANALYSIS FOR EXAMPLE, A CSU

00:20:37.202 --> 00:20:39.805
EMPLOYEE MADE INAPPROPRIATE

00:20:39.871 --> 00:20:40.906
COMMENTS TO A COMPLAINANT ABOUT

00:20:40.973 --> 00:20:42.541
HOW SHE DRESSED FREQUENTLY,

00:20:42.608 --> 00:20:43.542
HUGGED HER, AND INSTEAD OF

00:20:43.609 --> 00:20:45.611
SHAKING HANDS AND TOUCHED HER

00:20:45.677 --> 00:20:46.645
HAIR WHILE KISSING, ANOTHER

00:20:46.712 --> 00:20:48.714
STAFF MEMBER, THE INVESTIGATOR

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:49.581
CONCLUDED AGAIN THAT THIS

00:20:49.648 --> 00:20:51.817
ACTIVITY TOOK PLACE, BUT FOUND

00:20:51.883 --> 00:20:53.051
IT WAS NOT SUFFICIENTLY SEVERE,

00:20:53.118 --> 00:20:54.820
PERSISTENT OR PERVASIVE, IN PART

00:20:54.886 --> 00:20:56.488
BECAUSE THE COMPLAINANT WAS ABLE

00:20:56.555 --> 00:20:58.557
TO CONTINUE WORKING AND AVOID

00:20:58.624 --> 00:21:00.826
THE RESPONDENT, BUT WHEN WE

00:21:00.892 --> 00:21:01.994
LOOKED IN THE INVESTIGATION

00:21:02.060 --> 00:21:03.462
FILE, WE FOUND THAT THE

00:21:03.528 --> 00:21:04.763
INVESTIGATION REPORT NOTED THAT

00:21:04.830 --> 00:21:07.065
THEY OMITTED ANY ANALYSIS OF

00:21:07.132 --> 00:21:08.066
OTHER ALLEGATIONS OF

00:21:08.133 --> 00:21:10.335
INAPPROPRIATE TOUCHING, THAT THE

00:21:10.402 --> 00:21:11.336
COMPLAINANT AND OTHER WITNESSES

00:21:11.403 --> 00:21:13.572
BOTH TOLD THE INVESTIGATOR HAD

00:21:13.639 --> 00:21:15.774
OCCURRED. IN RESPONSE TO OUR

00:21:15.841 --> 00:21:16.908
CONCERNS OVER THE QUALITY OF ITS

00:21:16.975 --> 00:21:19.077
INVESTIGATION, CSU INDICATED

00:21:19.144 --> 00:21:20.212
THAT IT OFFERS TRAINING TO ITS

00:21:20.278 --> 00:21:21.380
TITLE NINE COORDINATORS AND

00:21:21.446 --> 00:21:22.914
PROVIDED MATERIALS WHICH IN OUR

00:21:22.981 --> 00:21:23.915
VIEW WERE REASONABLY DETAILED

00:21:23.982 --> 00:21:26.251
AND HELPFUL. BUT CSU OFFICIALS

00:21:26.318 --> 00:21:28.153
ACKNOWLEDGED THEY DON'T REQUIRE

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:29.154
THEIR COORDINATORS TO ATTEND

00:21:29.221 --> 00:21:30.956
THESE TRAININGS OR CONSULT THESE

00:21:31.023 --> 00:21:32.057
MATERIALS. IN OUR VIEW, MORE

00:21:32.124 --> 00:21:34.059
DETAILED GUIDANCE, SUCH AS

00:21:34.126 --> 00:21:35.027
WHAT'S PROVIDED IN THE

00:21:35.093 --> 00:21:36.862
TRAININGS, IS NECESSARY TO

00:21:36.928 --> 00:21:37.996
ENSURE CAMPUSES INVESTIGATE

00:21:38.063 --> 00:21:39.865
ALLEGATIONS CONSISTENTLY AND

00:21:39.931 --> 00:21:40.832
THOROUGHLY. AND WE ALSO BELIEVE

00:21:40.899 --> 00:21:43.068
THE CSU SHOULD DEVELOP A

00:21:43.135 --> 00:21:44.102
SECONDARY SUPERVISORY REVIEW

00:21:44.169 --> 00:21:45.937
PROCESS TO ENSURE INVESTIGATIONS

00:21:46.004 --> 00:21:48.940
ARE CONDUCTED IN A CONSISTENT

00:21:49.007 --> 00:21:52.310
MANNER. ANOTHER PROBLEM WITH THE

00:21:52.377 --> 00:21:53.445
INVESTIGATIONS IS WE OFTEN FOUND

00:21:53.512 --> 00:21:55.614
MISSING DOCUMENTATION IN 24 OF

00:21:55.681 --> 00:21:57.516
THE 40 CASES WE REVIEWED, WE

00:21:57.582 --> 00:21:59.217
NOTED THE ABSENCE OF EVIDENCE OF

00:21:59.284 --> 00:22:00.218
OUTREACH TO COMPLAINANTS AND

00:22:00.285 --> 00:22:01.753
POTENTIAL WITNESSES. WE NOTED

00:22:01.820 --> 00:22:04.556
THE ABSENCE OF RELEVANT EVIDENCE

00:22:04.623 --> 00:22:05.557
THAT WAS REFERRED TO IN THE

00:22:05.624 --> 00:22:07.559
INVESTIGATION, ABSENT INTERVIEW

00:22:07.626 --> 00:22:10.162
NOTES. AND OFTEN WE FOUND

00:22:10.228 --> 00:22:11.163
LACKING INFORMATION ON WHAT

00:22:11.229 --> 00:22:12.164
CORRECTIVE ACTIONS OR DISCIPLINE

00:22:12.230 --> 00:22:14.466
THE CSU IMPOSED, IF ANY, THAT

00:22:14.533 --> 00:22:16.234
WERE FOLLOWED FOLLOWING A

00:22:16.301 --> 00:22:18.937
FINDING OF A SUBSTANTIATED

00:22:19.004 --> 00:22:19.938
ALLEGATION OF SEXUAL HARASSMENT

00:22:20.005 --> 00:22:21.973
AT THE TIME OF OUR AUDIT, CSU

00:22:22.040 --> 00:22:24.609
DID NOT REQUIRE OR DID NOT

00:22:24.676 --> 00:22:27.145
ESTABLISH REQUIREMENTS SETTING

00:22:27.212 --> 00:22:27.579
EXPECTATIONS FOR HOW

00:22:27.646 --> 00:22:28.413
INVESTIGATORS SHOULD DOCUMENT

00:22:28.480 --> 00:22:30.382
THEIR CASEWORK. AGAIN, GOING

00:22:30.449 --> 00:22:33.085
BACK TO THE US DEPARTMENT OF

00:22:33.151 --> 00:22:34.019
JUSTICE, THEY NOTED THE

00:22:34.086 --> 00:22:36.388
IMPORTANCE OF SUCH REQUIREMENTS

00:22:36.455 --> 00:22:37.489
IN ITS 2021 RESOLUTION AGREEMENT

00:22:37.556 --> 00:22:40.258
WITH SAN JOSE STATE, WHICH

00:22:40.325 --> 00:22:41.660
REQUIRED THAT CAMPUS TO

00:22:41.727 --> 00:22:42.294
CONSISTENTLY DOCUMENT INTERVIEW

00:22:42.360 --> 00:22:44.396
NOTES, CORRESPONDENCE WITH THE

00:22:44.463 --> 00:22:47.099
PARTIES INVOLVED, AND ANY

00:22:47.165 --> 00:22:48.100
DISCIPLINARY ACTION THAT WAS

00:22:48.166 --> 00:22:50.936
TAKEN. WE BELIEVE THAT KIND OF

00:22:51.002 --> 00:22:51.970
STANDARD IS SOMETHING THAT

00:22:52.037 --> 00:22:53.138
SHOULD BE APPLIED SYSTEM WIDE.

00:22:53.205 --> 00:22:56.108
WE ALSO NOTED PROBLEMS WITH

00:22:56.174 --> 00:22:58.043
TIMELINESS, AND 13 OF THE 21

00:22:58.110 --> 00:22:59.077
INVESTIGATIONS WE REVIEWED, THEY

00:22:59.144 --> 00:23:01.046
WERE NOT COMPLETED WITHIN THE

00:23:01.113 --> 00:23:02.114
TIME FRAMES ESTABLISHED BY CSU

00:23:02.180 --> 00:23:04.216
POLICY. GENERALLY SPEAKING, CSU

00:23:04.282 --> 00:23:06.651
REQUIRES THAT THEIR

00:23:06.718 --> 00:23:07.219
INVESTIGATIONS BE COMPLETED

00:23:07.285 --> 00:23:09.688
WITHIN 100 AND WITHIN 100 DAYS.

00:23:09.755 --> 00:23:12.090
BUT WE NOTED THAT 13 OF THE 21

00:23:12.157 --> 00:23:13.625
INVESTIGATIONS THAT WE REVIEWED

00:23:13.692 --> 00:23:16.194
WERE OVER THIS MARK, RANGING

00:23:16.261 --> 00:23:18.396
FROM AS LITTLE AS 17 DAYS LATE,

00:23:18.463 --> 00:23:20.065
WHILE WE FOUND THREE THAT WERE

00:23:20.132 --> 00:23:21.233
OVER 200 DAYS LATE AND ONE

00:23:21.299 --> 00:23:23.568
INVESTIGATION, IT TOOK MORE THAN

00:23:23.635 --> 00:23:26.505
368 DAYS TO COMPLETE, AND WE

00:23:26.571 --> 00:23:27.739
NOTED IN THE CASE FILE THAT THE

00:23:27.806 --> 00:23:28.740
COMPLAINANT WAS EXTREMELY

00:23:28.807 --> 00:23:29.875
CONCERNED AND, QUOTE, JUST

00:23:29.941 --> 00:23:31.710
WANTED IT TO BE OVER. BUT THE

00:23:31.777 --> 00:23:34.579
CSU INVESTIGATOR EXTENDED THE

00:23:34.646 --> 00:23:35.147
INVESTIGATION FIVE DIFFERENT

00:23:35.213 --> 00:23:37.249
TIMES, CITING OTHER WORK

00:23:37.315 --> 00:23:37.716
COMMITMENTS OR NEEDING

00:23:37.783 --> 00:23:40.118
ADDITIONAL TIME TO PREPARE KEY

00:23:40.185 --> 00:23:42.154
DOCUMENTS. WE ALSO NOTED THAT

00:23:42.220 --> 00:23:44.022
ALL 13 CASES THAT WERE LATE, THE

00:23:44.089 --> 00:23:45.123
CASE FILES LACKED DOCUMENTATION

00:23:45.190 --> 00:23:46.057
TO DEMONSTRATE THAT THE PARTIES

00:23:46.124 --> 00:23:48.693
INVOLVED WERE INFORMED OF THE

00:23:48.760 --> 00:23:51.129
DELAYS ON A CONSISTENT BASIS OF

00:23:51.196 --> 00:23:52.297
THEIR CASES, AND WE RECOMMENDED

00:23:52.364 --> 00:23:53.431
THAT THE CHANCELLOR'S OFFICE

00:23:53.498 --> 00:23:55.801
